--- a/10_REQUIREMENTS/SMR014-PACKET-CONTRACT.md
+++ b/10_REQUIREMENTS/SMR014-PACKET-CONTRACT.md
@@ -10,11 +10,11 @@
 ## Portable implementation obligations
 1. Stream original bytes in one pass using fixed buffers; no canonical whole-file `readAllBytes`/`ByteArrayOutputStream` path.
 2. Capture only a bounded sniff prefix while streaming.
-3. Bind immutable request digest, expected SHA-256/size when supplied, declared media, deterministic detected media, governance, authorization and provenance refs.
+3. Bind immutable request digest, expected SHA-256/size when supplied, declared media, deterministic detected media, governance, authorization and provenance refs. Artifact request identity is globally unique, and the transfer identity tuple `(request_id, artifact_id, expected_sha256, expected_bytes)` may bind only one transfer ID; exact replay is idempotent only for the identical canonical object.
 4. Fail closed to QUARANTINED on digest/size/media/package-policy failure.
 5. Verified read APIs are streaming/ranged and require a durable VERIFIED receipt.
 6. ZIP/package inspection is non-extracting and rejects traversal, absolute/device/ADS-like paths, case/Unicode collisions, unknown sizes, entry/expanded/ratio limits and nested packages by default.
-7. Resumable transfer uses exact next offsets, bounded chunk sizes, per-chunk SHA-256, rolling digest, expected-byte reservation, terminal immutability and orphan partial reconciliation.
+7. Resumable transfer uses exact next offsets, bounded chunk sizes, per-chunk SHA-256, rolling digest, expected-byte reservation, terminal immutability and orphan partial reconciliation. Transfer request/artifact/work/expected-byte/expected-digest identity is immutable: begin parameters must agree with any request-declared expected size/digest, and completion must use the request identity bound when the transfer began. A transfer may complete only with the same request ID, artifact ID, work ID and supplied expected size/digest bound at begin; request substitution and same-transfer identity mutation fail closed.
 8. Content paths are server-generated from SHA-256; caller paths never choose storage destinations.
 9. No legacy public byte-ingest surface may mark a blob VERIFIED outside PLATFORM-008.
 10. Portable/static proof MUST NOT be represented as live filesystem/PostgreSQL/archive-corpus/storage-pressure proof.
